  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Danish annual contribution to UNRWA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensure that everyone everywhere can reach their full human potential and that all have access to fundamental human rights are overarching priorities of Denmark, as reflected in the Danish Development and Humanitarian Strategy. Denmark fully aligns itself with the goal of UNRWA&apos;s Medium-Term Strategy (MTS) for 2016-2021, which states that Palestine Refugees should 
lead long and healthy lives, are knowledgeable, have decent standard of living and enjoy human rights 
UNRWA&apos;s MTS describes five strategic outcomes of its core programmes, which Denmark supports:
1. Refugees&apos; rights under international law are protected and promoted
2. Refugees&apos; health is protected and the disease burden reduced
3. School-aged children complete quality, equitable and inclusive basic education 
4. Refugee capabilities are strengthened for increase livelihoods opportunities 
5. refugees are able to meet their basic human needs of food, shelter and environmental health 

Source: Strategy for Denmark&apos;s Engagement with UNRWA 2017-2021</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This allocation supports the core mandate of UNRWA. For further details on the achievements and results please visit: www.unrwa.org</narrative>
  </description>
